questions.explanation:
**Given:**

CB and BA are produced to CE and BD respectively

&ang;DAC = 110&deg;

&ang;ABE = 130&deg;

**Formula used:**

Exterior angle = Sum of interior opposite angles

Greater angle subtends greater side

**Calculations:**

&ang;DAC is exterior angle at A

&rArr; &ang;ABC + &ang;ACB = 110&deg;

&ang;ABE is exterior angle at B

&rArr; &ang;BAC + &ang;ACB = 130&deg;

Subtracting first from second

&rArr; (&ang;BAC + &ang;ACB) &minus; (&ang;ABC + &ang;ACB) = 130&deg; &minus; 110&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BAC &minus; &ang;ABC = 20&deg;

&rArr; &ang;BAC &gt; &ang;ABC

From &ang;ABC + &ang;ACB = 110&deg;

&rArr; &ang;ACB is the smallest angle

&rArr; &ang;ACB &lt; &ang;ABC &lt; &ang;BAC

&rArr; Opposite sides:

AB &lt; AC &lt; BC

**&there4; The correct option is: AB &lt; AC &lt; BC.**
